://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_Barnes\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... exuberant, coruscating translation.\\n\\n\\\"This is a luminous novel of India and Partition, but one whose spellbinding brio and fierce compassion weaves youth and age, male and female, family and nation into a kaleidoscopic whole.\\\"\\n\\nThe International Booker Prize 2022 Shortlist\\n\\n| Title | Author | Translator | Original Language | Author Residence | Publisher ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d48\"},\"ref\":\"d48\",\"snippet\":\" ... That it was ever even published – earning the first of her two Booker shortlistings, in 2012 – owed to the disillusionment of former Amazon employee Stefan Tobler, now 49, then working as a freelance translator assessing potential foreign-language acquisitions for a large literary imprint. When his proposal to ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d32\"},\"ref\":\"d32\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2019\\n\\nNo major changes for the press, but another good year for prize attention. Amy Arnold's Slip of a Fish landed a 2019 Goldsmiths Prize shortlisting, while Alia Trabucco Zerán's The Remainder was shortlisted for the Man Booker International Prize. Multiple translation prize wins and shortlistings ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"3e497e016c7aac8ebc700cea16f88e9d3ba91e00e840af0a2581078c97136b74\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"2f1bd873d7e11c508ea75ea50cccf37d3b9c6d07147e90fb68c3b0c3fa3d4fd3\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"The Fishermen 2015 Booker Prize shortlist translated languages\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_df14c0ccecd3421385ef1120"},{"content":"I have a strong lead. Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages.\n\nBut wait - the puzzle says the award was \"created in the 2000s.\" The Booker Prize was created in 1969. However, the Man Booker International Prize was inaugurated in 2005 (2000s). Let me reconsider.\n\nActually, let me re-read the puzzle: \"originally created in the 2000s (the award itself)\". This could mean the award was created in the 2000s. The Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005. But Obioma's books were shortlisted for the regular Booker Prize, not the International one.\n\nLet me reconsider the puzzle structure. The puzzle might be about a different award. Let me think about the \"preceding year\" clue: Book B won the award in the year Book A was published, but Book B was released the preceding year. \n\nLet me check the Man Booker International Prize winners in the 2010s and see if there's a book translated into 25+ languages that was a contender.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Booker International Prize winners list 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015\", \"International Booker Prize 2016 2017 2018 2019 winner\", \"book translated into 25 languages shortlisted International Booker Prize contender\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_d468be68a3fc4c3eadc4230a","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d3\"},\"ref\":\"d3\",\"snippet\":\" ... Readers' Poll, 1999\\n\\n2000-2010:\\n\\n- Best Local Author, NOW Magazine Readers' Poll, 2000\\n\\n- Winner Booker Prize for The Blind Assassin, 2000\\n\\n- Nominated for the Orange Prize, 2001\\n\\n- International Crimewriters Assocation Dashiell Hammett Award, 2001\\n\\n- Canadian Booksellers Association People's Choice Award, 2001\\n\\n- Short-listed for the IMPAC Dublin ... \",\"title\":\"https://margaretatwood.ca/awards-recognitions/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d36\"},\"ref\":\"d36\",\"snippet\":\" ... List 2012 . International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award 2012. Retrieved 23 January 2015.\\n* Financial Times 2010 Fiction of the YearBlau, Rosie (3 December 2010). FT Fiction Round-up 2010. Financial Times, Fiction Round-up 2010. Retrieved 25 January 2015.\\n\\nLife of Pi\\n\\n* Winner of the 2002 Man Booker Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yann_Martel\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d25\"},\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... list of winners and shortlisted authors of the Booker Prize for Fiction. The prize has been awarded each year since 1969 to the best original full-length novel, written in the English language, by a citizen of the Commonwealth of Nations or the Republic of Ireland. In 2014 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her work has won the Nobel Prize in Literature, two Scotiabank Giller Prizes, three Governor General's Literary Awards and the Man Booker International Prize. Her first book, Dance of the Happy Shades, was released in 1968, and she continued to write stories until retiring in 2013.\\n\\nWachtel ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2010 | Howard Jacobson | The Finkler Question | Comic novel | |\\n| 2011 | Julian Barnes | The Sense of an Ending | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2012 | Hilary Mantel | Bring Up the Bodies | Historical fiction | |\\n| 2013 | Eleanor Catton | The Luminaries | Historical fiction | |\\n| 2014 | Richard Flanagan | The Narrow Road to the Deep North | Historical fiction | |\\n| 2015 | Marlon ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... companion, longlisted for the 2011 International Dublin Literary Award)\\n* MaddAddam (2013) (Third novel in Oryx and Crake trilogy)\\n* Scribbler Moon (written in 2014 as part of the Future Library project; will remain unpublished until 2114)\\n* The Heart Goes Last (2015) (Winner of the 2015 Red Tentacle award)\\n* Hag ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... winner of the 2012 Green Rose Prize in Poetry from New Issues Press), Carrier Wave (winner of the 2006 Colorado Prize for Poetry from the Center for Literary Publishing at Colorado State University), and the digital chapbook The Tallest Building in America (Floating Wolf Quarterly 2014). An international ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsandsciences.syracuse.edu/english-department/creative-writing-mf-program/raymond-carver-reading-series/previous-raymond-carver-reading-series/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... have been awarded 34 Pulitzer Prizes, 12 National Book Awards, 30 National Book Critics Circle Awards, 6 Man Booker Prizes, and 3 Nobel Prizes. In 2011, the London Book Fair presented him with a Lifetime Achievement Award for his work in international publishing.\\n\\nBorn in India in 1942 ... \",\"title\":\"https://centerforfiction.org/grants-awards/medal-for-editorial-excellence/medal-for-editorial-excellence-past-recipients/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"6fc3abe2b3ccf76fb51827224a703013e242d09abf1f6374994835c4b9d08998\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"2813d0e3a3bc9ea1ca60874cae5512b9822e67145700d2dfc8cc6dd6cac8845c\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker International Prize winners list 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d3\"},\"ref\":\"d3\",\"snippet\":\" ... Award, 2017\\n\\n- Raymond Chandler Award, 2017\\n\\n- Academy Board of Directors' Tribute, 2018\\n\\n- UCD Ulysses Medal, 2018\\n\\n- Adrienne Clarkson Prize for Global Citizenship, 2018\\n\\n- Order of the Companions of Honour,